---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { tasks } from "../lib/tasks";
import pilot from "../../../results/exp001/exp001.json";

const formatInt = (n: number) => Math.round(n).toLocaleString("en-US");
const formats = pilot.summary.map(item => {
  const rows = pilot.runs.filter(run => run.config.micro_batch_size === item.micro_batch_size && run.status === "ok");
  return {
    ...item,
    completed: rows.length,
    memory: rows.length ? Math.max(...rows.map(run => run.peak_allocated_gb)) : null,
    accumulation: rows[0]?.config.grad_accum_steps ?? null,
  };
});
const best = formats.filter(row => row.status === "accepted" && row.speedup !== null)
  .reduce<number>((max, row) => Math.max(max, row.speedup ?? 0), 0);
---
<BaseLayout title="Experiments">
  <div class="eyebrow">Experiments / Measured pilot</div>
  <h1>What changed when the micro-batch got larger?</h1>
  <p class="lead">EXP-001 is our first measured Kaggle pilot, using synthetic tokens and a small causal Transformer. It compares three configurations on one Tesla T4 GPU while keeping tokens per optimizer step fixed.</p>
  <div class="grid">
    <section class="card"><div class="muted small">Best observed pilot speedup</div><div class="metric">{best.toFixed(2)}×</div><span class="chip">Against micro-batch 4</span></section>
    <section class="card"><div class="muted small">Completed trial runs</div><div class="metric">{pilot.runs.filter(run => run.status === "ok").length}/{pilot.runs.length}</div><span class="chip">{pilot.workload.repeats} seeds per configuration</span></section>
    <section class="card"><div class="muted small">Hardware</div><div class="metric" style="font-size:1.6rem">{pilot.hardware.gpu}</div><span class="chip">One GPU used</span></section>
  </div>
  <section class="card">
    <h2>Measured training throughput</h2>
    <p class="muted small">Median CUDA-event tokens/second; higher is better. Bar lengths are proportional to the fastest measured configuration.</p>
    {formats.map(row => <div style="margin:20px 0">
      <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <strong>Micro-batch {row.micro_batch_size}</strong>
        <span>{row.median_tps === undefined ? "Incomplete" : formatInt(row.median_tps)} tokens/sec</span>
      </div>
      <div style="height:13px;background:var(--soft);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;margin:9px 0" role="img" aria-label={`Micro-batch ${row.micro_batch_size}: ${row.median_tps ? formatInt(row.median_tps) : "no"} tokens per second`}>
        <div style={`height:100%;background:var(--blue);border-radius:10px;width:${row.median_tps ? (100 * row.median_tps / Math.max(...formats.map(r => r.median_tps ?? 0))).toFixed(1) : 0}%`}></div>
      </div>
      <p class="muted small" style="margin:0">Accumulation: {row.accumulation ?? "—"} · Peak allocated memory: {row.memory?.toFixed(3) ?? "—"} GB · Speedup: {row.speedup?.toFixed(2) ?? "—"}× · {row.completed} successful runs</p>
    </div>)}
    <p class="small muted">All three configurations satisfied this pilot's loss and timing checks. Each candidate processed {pilot.workload.tokens_per_step.toLocaleString("en-US")} tokens per optimizer step.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="card" style="margin-top:20px">
    <h2>How should we interpret this?</h2>
    <p>Increasing the micro-batch reduced the number of gradient accumulation passes required for an optimizer step. This may reduce overhead, but it increased measured peak GPU memory.</p>
    <p><strong>Limitations:</strong> This is exploratory evidence only: {pilot.workload.timed_steps} timed optimizer steps per run, {pilot.workload.repeats} seeds, fixed synthetic data, and one GPU. The checks are not an independent security boundary. We have not tested the full GPT-2 benchmark or whether an LLM agent's gains generalize to held-out hardware.</p>
    <p class="small"><a href="https://github.com/mbzuaiciao/throughput-agent/blob/main/results/exp001/exp001.json">Inspect the source results JSON</a></p>
  </section>
  <hr />
  <h2>Planned benchmark tasks</h2>
  <p class="muted">The following task definitions describe future research experiments. They are separate from the completed Kaggle pilot.</p>
  <div class="grid">
    {tasks.map(task => <section class="card">
      <span class="chip">{task.split.replaceAll("_", " ")}</span>
      <h2 style="margin-top:14px">{task.model}</h2>
      <p><strong>{task.n_gpus} × {task.gpu_type}</strong> · {task.seq_len.toLocaleString()} tokens/sequence</p>
      <p class="small muted">{task.global_batch_tokens.toLocaleString()} tokens per optimizer step · {task.attempt_budget} proposals allowed</p>
      <p class="small muted">Task ID: <code>{task.task_id}</code></p>
    </section>)}
  </div>
  <p class="small muted">This is a static, read-only view of committed data. It does not initiate Kaggle or cloud jobs.</p>
</BaseLayout>
